{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerSymmetry","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerSymmetry","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerLobachevsky"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_lob_conj_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_lob_conj_inv","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L222-L233","doc":"**`D(conj (1/z)) = D(z)`** — the two orientation reversals compose back to\nthe identity on `D`.\n\nThis is the step that connects Ohtsuki's shape `y₀` (a root of `y³ − 3y² + 2y −\n1` in the *upper* half plane) to the corpus's triangulation shape `y₊` (a root\nof the reciprocal cubic `y³ − 2y² + 3y − 1`, also upper): the reciprocal drops\ninto the lower half plane, and conjugation lifts it back. Measured,\n`y₊ = 0.7849201454990266… + 1.3071412786820454…i = conj (1/y₀)`, and both give\n`D = 0.9427073627769277…`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_lob_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_lob_conj","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L201-L220","doc":"**`D` is odd under conjugation**: `D(z̄) = −D(z)` for `z` off the real axis.\n\nConjugation commutes with all three Möbius maps (`1 − z̄ = conj (1 − z)`,\n`1/(1 − z̄) = conj (1/(1 − z))`, `1 − 1/z̄ = conj (1 − 1/z)`), because they have\n*real* coefficients. So each angle is negated in place and `Λ` is odd.\n\nThis is the formal content of the remark in `FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge` that the\nconjugation half of the two-cubic reconciliation is `D(z̄) = −D(z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.arg_conj_of_im_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.arg_conj_of_im_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L196-L199","doc":"`arg z̄ = −arg z` off the real axis, discharging the same branch-cut `if`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_lob_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_lob_inv","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L162-L186","doc":"**`D` is odd under inversion**: `D(1/z) = −D(z)` for `z` off the real axis.\n\nUnder `z ↦ 1/z` the three shape parameters go to their own reciprocals, but\n*shuffled*: `1/z`'s first angle is minus `z`'s first, its second is minus `z`'s\nthird, and its third is minus `z`'s second. Concretely\n`1 − 1/(1/z) = 1 − z` and `1/(1 − 1/z)` is the reciprocal of `z`'s third shape.\nSo the sum is again a reordering, this time of three negated terms.\n\nThe hypothesis `z.im ≠ 0` is exactly what keeps all three reciprocals off the\n`arg` branch cut; it cannot be dropped, since at a real `z` the identity reads\n`0 = −0` only because both sides vanish for a different reason\n(`BlochWigner_lob_real_eq_zero`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.one_div_im_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.one_div_im_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L154-L160","doc":"`1/z` is off the real axis when `z` is: `Im z⁻¹ = −Im z / |z|²`. Needed three\ntimes below, and again in the `5₂` bridge, because every `hbw`-style hypothesis\nabout a dilogarithm has to be applied at both `z` and `1/z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.arg_one_div_of_im_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.arg_one_div_of_im_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L150-L152","doc":"`arg (1/z) = −arg z` off the real axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.arg_ne_pi_of_im_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.arg_ne_pi_of_im_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L143-L148","doc":"`arg z ≠ π` off the real axis. Mathlib's `Complex.arg_inv` and `arg_conj`\nboth carry an `if arg z = π` guard for the branch cut; this is the side\ncondition that discharges it, and it is the *only* thing `z.im ≠ 0` is used for\nbelow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.blochWigner_xOf_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.blochWigner_xOf_eq","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L123-L133","doc":"**Lemma (i) of the `5₂` bridge.** With `x₀ = 1 − 1/y₀`, the two shapes have\nthe same Bloch–Wigner value. Verified numerically at 40 digits\n(`D(x₀) − D(y₀) = 1.1e-41`) before it was proved; here it is a corollary of the\ncyclic symmetry, and needs no `5₂`-specific input at all.\n\nThis is one of the facts `FiveTwoOhtsukiBridge.ohtsuki_sum_im_eq_three_blochWigner`\nrests on. The others are `BlochWigner_lob_inv` below and an `arg`–`log`\ncancellation which, once the cubic is used, is three `arg` evaluations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_lob_mobius_cycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWigner_lob_mobius_cycle","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L113-L121","doc":"**`D` is invariant under the order-3 Möbius rotation `z ↦ 1 − 1/z`.**\n\nThe proof is a reordering: the three Lobachevsky summands are permuted\ncyclically, so the sum is unchanged. Nothing is evaluated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tetAngle₃_mobius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tetAngle₃_mobius","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L105-L109","doc":"`tetAngle₃` of the rotated shape is `tetAngle₂` of the original. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tetAngle₂_mobius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tetAngle₂_mobius","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L99-L103","doc":"`tetAngle₂` of the rotated shape is `tetAngle₁` of the original. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tetAngle₁_mobius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tetAngle₁_mobius","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L95-L97","doc":"`tetAngle₁` of the rotated shape is `tetAngle₃` of the original —\ndefinitionally, since both are `(1 − 1/z).arg`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.one_sub_inv_mobius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.one_sub_inv_mobius","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L73-L91","doc":"Under `w = 1 − 1/z`, the third shape parameter returns `1/(1−z)`.\n\nNote the shape of the proof: rewrite `1 − 1/z` as `(z−1)/z` **first**, so the\nnested division becomes a single quotient and `field_simp` has the non-vanishing\nfacts it needs already in hand. Trying to `field_simp` the nested form directly\nasks it to discharge `1 − 1/z ≠ 0` on its own.\n\n**Both** orientations of the non-vanishing fact have to be in context. `field_simp`\nmatches hypotheses syntactically, so `z − 1 ≠ 0` does not discharge the `(1 − z)⁻¹`\nthat the right-hand side contributes: with only that one, the goal reduces to\n`-1 = z * (1 - z)⁻¹ - (1 - z)⁻¹` and stalls there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.inv_one_sub_mobius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.inv_one_sub_mobius","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L66-L71","doc":"Under `w = 1 − 1/z`, the second shape parameter returns `z` itself.\nThis is the step that closes the 3-cycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.one_sub_mobius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.one_sub_mobius","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerSymmetry.lean#L63-L64","doc":"Under `w = 1 − 1/z`, the \"one minus\" slot returns `1/z`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}